<%- include("partials/public-shell-start", { pageTitle }) %>

<section class="legal-page">
  <div class="legal-hero">
    <span class="legal-hero__badge">Election Portal Policy</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong><%= settings.electionName %></strong>
      collects, uses, protects, and stores information for voting, nominations,
      observer access, and election administration.
    </p>
    <small>Last updated: July 4, 2026</small>
  </div>

  <div class="legal-layout">
    <aside class="legal-summary-card">
      <h2>Quick Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Staff details are used only for election eligibility and verification.</li>
        <li>Each voter can vote only once.</li>
        <li>Vote choices are protected and not displayed publicly with voter names.</li>
        <li>Admins can access records only for election operations and audit purposes.</li>
        <li>Contact support if you need help with your data or account access.</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <article class="legal-document">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
          The portal may collect staff ID, full name, phone number, department,
          voter status, nomination information, candidate photos, observer details,
          admin login activity, audit logs, device information, and timestamps.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>
          We use information to verify eligible voters, prevent duplicate voting,
          manage nominations, send OTP or election SMS messages, support observer
          monitoring, generate reports, and maintain a trusted election audit trail.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Voting Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The system is designed so that public results show totals and winners,
          not a public list of how individual staff voted. Election administrators
          must use any internal election records only for official audit, security,
          backup, and dispute-resolution purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. OTP, SMS, and Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          The portal may use trusted services such as SMS gateways, hosting
          providers, CAPTCHA protection, and domain/security providers to operate
          the system. These services may process limited technical information
          needed to deliver OTP codes, protect forms, and keep the portal online.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Cookies and Sessions</h2>
        <p>
          The portal uses secure session cookies to keep voters, observers, and
          administrators signed in during their current activity. These cookies
          help protect the process and are not used for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          Access controls, admin authentication, audit logs, CAPTCHA checks, OTP
          verification, database backups, and role-based pages help protect the
          election data. No system is perfect, but reasonable technical and
          administrative controls are used to reduce risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Election records may be kept after an election for reporting, archives,
          audit, dispute review, and legal or organizational accountability. The
          election committee or authorized IT team may reset active election data
          when preparing for a new election, while preserving archived results
          where required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          Staff should keep their staff ID, phone number, OTP, application number,
          and login credentials private. Do not share codes or attempt to access
          another person's record.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or support, contact
          <a href="mailto:jacksmeg99@gmail.com">jacksmeg99@gmail.com</a>
          or call <a href="tel:+233592934612">0592934612</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="legal-note">
        This page is provided for operational transparency. The organization may
        update this policy when election processes, security settings, or service
        providers change.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include("partials/public-shell-end") %>
